<div class="bg-surface border border-rule rounded-[3px] p-6">
	<h3 class="text-xl font-medium text-ink mb-4">Challenge your thinking — Delegation</h3>
	<dl class="flex flex-col gap-4">
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">A · Activating Event</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					What just happened?
				</span>
				I see a mistake happening on a task I've already delegated. My instinct
				is to take it back and do it myself.
			</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">B · Beliefs</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					What am I telling myself must happen?
				</span>
				Why isn't this person taking this as seriously as I do? If this doesn't
				get done right it reflects on me — and that means I'm not as competent
				as I need to be.
			</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">C · Consequences</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					What is that belief making me feel and do?
				</span>
				A flash of frustration, and the urge to step in and take the work
				back right now.
			</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">D · Disputing</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					Where is the evidence for that belief?
				</span>
				Where is it written that delegated work has to go right the first
				time? A mistake getting corrected is not a verdict on how I lead —
				it's just a mistake getting corrected.
			</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">E · Effective Thinking</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					What's a truer way to see it?
				</span>
				I hope they take this as seriously as I do, but if they don't, it's not
				the end of the world. My job is to develop people, not to do their work
				for them — and their mistake doesn't decide whether I'm good at mine.
			</dd>
		</div>
		<div>
			<dt class="eyebrow text-muted mb-1">F · Feeling &amp; Practice</dt>
			<dd class="text-ink">
				<span class="block text-muted text-base italic mb-1">
					What will I do right now?
				</span>
				I take ten seconds to picture myself handling it calmly. Then I have a
				brief, specific conversation about what needs correcting and why, and
				I'm clear about the standard. I give them 24 hours to fix it — and I
				don't check in before then.
			</dd>
		</div>
	</dl>
</div>
